  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>The Carlton, with its unmistakable domes, has been one of the symbols of the Croisette since 1911. A historic palace hotel, private beach, view over the Bay of Cannes: a stay here is above all an exceptional experience.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you book</h2>
      <p>The hotel's official website (carltoncannes.com) does not display a pet policy in the pages consulted. The booking listings agree on the principle: pets admitted on request, dogs and cats only, at 100 € per animal per day (Expedia, Trip.com), with assistance animals exempt from fees and water and food bowls available (Expedia). The Michelin Guide notes "pets admitted, charges may apply".</p>
      <p>The weight limit comes only from unofficial sources: BringFido states 1 dog of 8 kg maximum per room, and a reply attributed to the hotel on the Cityhotel page says pets under 8 kg are admitted at 100 € per day but cannot go to the beach or the restaurant, except on the Riviera terrace. Parking is paid (90 € per day according to the Michelin Guide).</p>
      <p>Check before booking: dog admission, the supplement, the weight limit and the prohibited areas should be confirmed directly with the hotel (04 93 06 40 06); they rest here on booking platforms.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: at this level of service, a phone call before booking lets you get written confirmation of the accepted size, the rate and the areas where your dog can go (private beach, restaurants, terrace).</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Croisette and its gardens are well suited to a leashed walk, and Cannes harbour is just a few minutes' walk away.</p>
    </div>

